L0243: Fields do not satisfy a derived trait

A derive cannot establish its promise for a field or payload. Copy needs copyable payloads; Logical aggregates need logical stored fields. Physical Box remains physical even when its payload is logical. Change the representation or derive only supported traits.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/copy_with_non_copy_field.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```rust
// A struct or an enum is `Copy` only if every field is: a field whose type
// does not derive `Copy` prevents it, and is named. `Clone` asks the same
// of its fields, and a tuple field has what its parts have.
#[derive(Clone)]
struct Token {
    id: u8,
}

struct Opaque {
    id: u8,
}

#[derive(Clone, Copy)]
struct Pair {
    left: Token,
    tag: u8,
}

#[derive(Clone, Copy)]
enum Slot {
    Empty,
    Full(Token),
}

#[derive(Clone)]
struct Holder {
    inner: (u8, Opaque),
}
```

Language, as built: [1.5:3](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.5:3).
